     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is double the FDA-labeled maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1000 mg per dose. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease check which of these you meant:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **1700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** If 1700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it.\n\nOnce you tell me which one, I'll enter it right away."
      }
